'' WHAT fbc's fb DIALECT REFUSES, tiko refuses (T86) -- fbc's error 146, "Only valid in
'' -lang deprecated or fblite or qb", as TKO0409 naming the keyword, and TKO0944 for a
'' numbered line. 'let', 'lprint', 'option' and '$include' compiled with no diagnostic,
'' 'on k gosub' reached clang, and 'call', 'defint' and a numbered line were refused with
'' TKO0408, TKO0743 and TKO0420. See src/parser/intrinsics.bas, LegacyStatement_.
''
'' MEASURED, fbc-modern 1.20 with -maxerr inf over the source, 2026-10-03: error 146 on
'' exactly lines 2 and 11-19, and 24 on 22 -- one report per line, the second numbered line
'' included. 'let ( a, b ) = pp' (20) is the fb dialect's own LET and stays legal, and
'' ': 0 = 1' (22) is a literal target, not a line number.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/fb-dialect-refusals.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb-dialect-refusals.bas(2,2): error TKO0409: '$INCLUDE' is not available in the fb dialect
